<title>USA: Payless Cashways to close nine stores.</title>
<headline>Payless Cashways to close nine stores.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payless Cashways Inc said Tuesday it plans to close nine underperforming stores, for which it took an after-tax store closing charge of $8.5 million in the August 24 third quarter.</p>
<p>The building materials specialty retailer also said its lenders agreed in principle to amend Payless Cashways' 1995 Credit Agreement to revise certain terms and to extend and increase available credit.</p>
</text>
